      "result": "All 22 checklist items have been executed and recorded — testing is complete.\n\n**Summary: 17 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core bookkeeping flows work well: transaction creation with full field set, search by description/reference, combined filtering, category CRUD, tax marking and its propagation into the annual tax summary, category rollups, printing, and dashboard/report totals.\n\nFive defects were found:\n\n- **FT-7** — The Edit Transaction form fails to pre-populate the existing category. Editing any other field and saving silently wipes the category, causing unintended data loss.\n- **CS-23** — No missing-category validation; a transaction saved with no category at all and no error shown.\n- **CS-24** — Deleting a category that has transactions is neither blocked nor offers reassignment, orphaning transactions with a blank category.\n- **CS-15** — A reversed date range (From later than To) is accepted silently, showing only a generic \"No transactions found\" rather than flagging the invalid range.\n- **IX-16** — Dashboard \"Total Balance\" is static ($74,931 through add/edit/delete, and inconsistent with the underlying $11,106.51 net), though all other summaries update immediately.\n- **CT-22** — Chart Y-axis labels are formatted in whole thousands, so a $320.50 bar renders full-height against five \"$0k\" ticks.\n\nNote: testing left two intentional side effects in the app's in-memory state — the \"Software\" category was deleted (as required by CS-24), leaving its Adobe CC transaction uncategorized. All other test data was cleaned up.",
